    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d623">

                <pb facs="0688" n="430" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg430"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 300.115/3523</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at London</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Skinner</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-06-02">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 2, 1915</hi>.</date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 3.30 p. m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Board Trade has agreed to advance fivepence per pound on certain cotton <hi
                        rendition="#italic">ex Livonia</hi> and <hi rendition="#italic">Dicido</hi>.
                    Advances in these cases indicate that on presentation of satisfactory documents
                    other similar advances will be made.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Skinner</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
